# Dataset and verification

Selected source: [TheStatsDontLie — World Cup 2026, Fixtures / Results / Match Stats](https://www.thestatsdontlie.com/football/world-cup-2026/). It is the approved parent source recorded in the existing Objective 1 project. This source provides the needed shots and shots-on-target columns; a score-only dataset would not suffice.

[Published sheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/2PACX-1vSWZFlaUHTBK09v4I1Kv7ZQ0ophhlpsCr7VPFW5dkbdG0Zpl8mRkXrTZezZMr1Ia9V9cpwmq7BKPQ03/pubhtml?gid=995472238&single=true)

[Direct CSV export](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/2PACX-1vSWZFlaUHTBK09v4I1Kv7ZQ0ophhlpsCr7VPFW5dkbdG0Zpl8mRkXrTZezZMr1Ia9V9cpwmq7BKPQ03/pub?gid=995472238&single=true&output=csv)

Downloaded on 8 September 2026, Darwin local date (7 September UTC). The original export is preserved without edits at `data/raw/published_world_cup.csv`.

SHA-256: `5b3420416acaf1cd65b8beec80eef4f06e99ead9c89135a000ed38be8609cb1b`.

The export contains multiple sections. This task validates and analyses only the 72 group-stage rows. Completeness of the knockout sections is not asserted. Dates are retained as displayed by the source; do not assume they are venue-local dates or UTC kickoff timestamps.

## Field mapping (zero-based CSV positions)

| Positions | Fields |
|---|---|
| 0 | Date |
| 1, 4 | Team 1, Team 2 |
| 22, 23 | Shots, Team 1 and Team 2 |
| 24, 25 | Shots on target, Team 1 and Team 2 |

`source_row` is the logical CSV record number, including the three heading records. It is not a physical text line number: the shots-on-target heading includes a newline.

## Verification achieved

The saved older browser capture is included as `data/raw/previous_group_stage_capture.tsv`, SHA-256 `e9c5ae8f09bd22f42379a4442ba883e73c664a3bb3fe0937b917c955b46ac2fc`. Dates, team order, and all **288 shot-count values** agree exactly with the direct export. Every accuracy is recomputed; no previously calculated percentages are trusted. Tests independently verify ratios using exact fractions, the slope formula against SciPy, retention of all matches and a t interval against SciPy.

An opening-match spot check against [FIFA's Mexico–South Africa report](https://www.fifatrainingcentre.com/media/native/tournaments/fifa-world-cup/2026/PMSR-M01%20MEX%20V%20RSA.pdf) also agrees on the four shot values: 16 and 3 attempts, 4 and 2 on target. This is one match, not verification of all 72 against FIFA.

## Limits

Agreement with the published source verifies transcription/extraction, not underlying event accuracy. Detailed provider rules for blocked shots, woodwork and other event classifications have not been independently verified. Use the columns consistently as published and acknowledge provider definitions. No invented results, simulated tournament data or borrowed future values are included. Retain attribution; no blanket redistribution licence is asserted for the provider's data. The snapshot is supplied for the requested assignment analysis.
